From ffd3173e0a4520539819740ccce92b1c7ed706ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:06:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cpu: AVX2 kernels for the Q8_0 4x8 repack (x86)

Upstream selects the Q8_0 repack only on NEON/RISC-V; on x86 Q8_0 weights use the plain
ggml_vec_dot_q8_0_q8_0 (one row, one accumulator). This adds AVX2 GEMV/GEMM kernels for
block_q8_0x4 (4 interleaved rows, 8-byte chunks) and selects q8_0_4x8 on AVX2 when ne[1] % 4 == 0.
MAG_NO_Q8_0_REPACK=1 disables the selection at runtime (A/B).

Results identical to the reference path (max rel. error ~1e-7, float summation order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch-fallback.h     |   4 +-
 ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/repack.cpp | 119 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp          |   8 ++
 3 files changed, 129 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

